  "live_records": {
    "q-48709": {
      "dom_id": "step-q48709",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The function $V(t)$ models the number of visitors, in thousands, to a new website, $t$ hours after the website's launch. What is the best interpretation of the statement below?\n\n$\\,$ *The slope of the tangent line to the graph of $V(t)$ at $t=10$ is equal to $1.5.$*",
      "worked_solution": "The slope of the line tangent to the graph of $V(t)$ at $t=10$ gives the derivative of $V(t)$ at $t=10.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n{V}^{′}(10)=1.5.\n$$\n\nWe can interpret the above statement as\n\n$\\,$ *$10$ hours after launching, the number of visitors increased at a rate of $1\\,500$ visitors per hour.*",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
