    "q-72106": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72106",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Joseph is measuring the weight gain of his pet puppy by recording the following two numbers for different values of $t,$ where $t$ is the time, in days, since he started his observations:\n\n- $W(t)$ - The puppy's weight, in kilograms\n\n- $r(t)$ - the rate at which the puppy's weight is increasing.\n\nWhat is the relationship between $W(t)$ and $r(t)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The function $W(t)$ gives the weight of the puppy after $t$ days. Then,\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}W(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }W}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${W}^{′}(t)$ gives the rate at which the weight of the puppy increases at time $t$, which is the same as $r(t).$ Therefore, the relationship between $W(t)$ and $r(t)$ is ${W}^{′}(t)=r(t).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
